      "role": "user",
      "content": "Wait, did you just say \"adventures\" and \"escapades\"? I'm not on an adventure, I'm in a repair shop trying to prevent a fire from starting. This is actually really frustrating. \n\nCan we please stick to the actual science? I need to know specifically: what is the physical mechanism that causes the temperature to drop right when the gas release starts? Is it an endothermic reaction? And how does that relate to the thermal runaway risk? I need the real technical details, not the stories.",
